"funny_loss_text": "",
"hook": "keeps a hand pressed to a crude, half-healed wound {subj} clearly hasn't had looked at properly",
"is_combat": true,
"success_reveal": "\"Wolves took the last of our flock, then came back for us,\" {subj_cap} admits. \"Drove the whole village off. I got clear. Not sure how many others did.\" The pack itself has drawn attention — something's been trailing {poss} scent for a while now, and it's close."
}, {
"combat_monster_names": Array[String]([]),
"funny_loss_text": "{subj_cap} glances once more down the road and decides silence is safer than an answer. \"Better you don't know,\" {subj} says, pulling {poss} pack a little closer, and says nothing further no matter how you press.",
"hook": "keeps {poss} voice carefully quiet, glancing at the road in both directions before speaking",
"is_combat": false,
"success_reveal": "\"Reeve's men,\" {subj_cap} says finally. \"Burned the village for harbouring a deserter — one man, and they burned the whole place for it. I wasn't the deserter. Didn't matter.\" There's no fixing that with coin or a kind word, only the simple, real relief of being believed."
}, {
"combat_monster_names": Array[String]([]),
"funny_loss_text": "{subj_cap} opens {poss} mouth, then closes it again, whatever the answer is plainly too raw to hand to a stranger. \"Alone. That's all there is to it,\" {subj} says, and the flatness in {poss} voice makes clear there's nothing more coming.",
"hook": "won't quite explain why {subj}'s travelling entirely alone",
"is_combat": false,
"success_reveal": "\"There isn't anyone else,\" {subj_cap} says eventually, quiet and flat in the particular way of someone who's said it enough times to stop it hurting on the way out. \"Flux took the rest of us over the winter. I'm what's left.\" {subj_cap} doesn't want pity, particularly — just doesn't want to be alone in the telling of it, for once."
}, {
"combat_monster_names": Array[String]([]),
"funny_loss_text": "{subj_cap} tucks {poss} hands away, out of sight, whatever {subj} almost said swallowed back down with them. \"Doesn't matter how I got here,\" {subj} says, quiet and closed, and won't be drawn any further on it.",
"hook": "keeps glancing at {poss} own hands like {subj} doesn't recognize them anymore",
"is_combat": false,
"success_reveal": "\"Wasn't always like this,\" {subj_cap} admits, gesturing vaguely at {poss}self — the rags, the road, all of it. \"Had a farm. Had a name people used without spitting after it. The harvest failed twice running and the debt did the rest.\" {subj_cap}'s grateful for nothing more than being spoken to like a person again."
}, {
"combat_monster_names": Array[String]([]),
